course: dictionary
lesson: 6172
title: Big words in government and church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ministry is a part of the government that looks after one big job for the whole country, such as health or schools. You can work out which job from the words around it. «The Ministry of Education opened ten new libraries this year.» Schools and libraries are about education, so the ministry must be the team that runs education.
explain: Ministry has a second meaning, linked to religion. «She felt called to the ministry after years of helping at her church.» Here the clue is the church. A ministry in this sense is the work of a priest or minister.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «The Ministry of Health said the water was safe to drink», the words "the team that runs health" still make sense. If your meaning does not fit, read on or look the word up.
fact: A ministry is a department of government led by a minister.
fact: «Ministry of Health» means the part of government that looks after people's health.
fact: «Ministry of Defence» means the part of government that looks after the country's armed forces.
fact: In religion, «the ministry» means the work of a priest or minister.
fact: Ministry is a noun, and its plural is ministries.
exercise: «The Ministry of Education opened ten new libraries this year.» What is a ministry in this sentence? | *A department of government that runs education | A type of school uniform | A long, slow walk | A kind of library book
exercise: «She felt called to the ministry after years of helping at her church.» What does ministry mean here? | A type of musical instrument | A small shop that sells bread | *The work of a priest or minister in a church | A government department for roads
exercise: Jayden says a ministry is a kind of shop. Is he right? | *No, it is a part of government or the work of a church leader | Yes, it is a type of bird | No, it is a kind of car | Yes, it sells food and drink
test: «The Ministry of Defence looks after the armed forces.» Which job does this ministry do? | Grows vegetables for schools | *Looks after the country's armed forces | Keeps the parks tidy | Runs the post office
test: «He spent five years in the ministry before he retired.» What does ministry mean here? | *The time someone spends working as a government or religious minister | A hospital ward for children | A lake in the hills | A school trip to a museum
exam: Which is the plural of ministry? | ministrees | *ministries | ministrys | ministers
